{
  "id": "hydraulic_cylinder_area_vs__diameter",
  "title": "Hydraulic Cylinder Area vs. Diameter",
  "description": "Calculate the acting area of a hydraulic cylinder based on its diameter. Typical hydraulic cylinders and acting area vs. cylinder diameter.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Hydraulic Cylinder Area vs. Diameter\n\nTypical hydraulic cylinders and acting area vs. cylinder diameter.\n\n![hydraulic cylinder](static/docs/documents/1466/hydraulic_cylinder.png \"hydraulic cylinder\")\n\nThe acting area of a hydraulic cylinder is calculated using the formula: **A = π × (d/2)²**, where d is the cylinder diameter.\n\n_1 in (inch) = 25.4 mm_"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "diameter",
          "label": "Cylinder Diameter",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "in",
          "defaultValue": 2
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "area",
          "label": "Cylinder Area",
          "formula": "3.14159 * (inputs.diameter / 2) ** 2",
          "unit": "in²",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
